BIOS validates usable E820 RAM across1..16MiB, keeps the old stack pool1..4MiB,
loads the bundle at4..5MiB and reserves8..16MiB as application workspace.
Each32KiB optical read uses the low bounce region20000..27fff, then an owned
INT15/AH87 descriptor table at6800 copies it upward. The selected kernel is
loaded at20000 only after the entire bundle has been copied. The64-bit slot
ends at93fff (475136 bytes); the32-bit slot ends at9bfff (507904 bytes).
UEFI loads TOOLS.BIN from the same FAT root and allocates its bundle/workspace
with boot services; IA32 requires all end addresses below its4GiB guard.
The kernel validates this handoff and every selected application before entry.

Bundle storage revision for0.12
Application slots grow to156KiB (159744 bytes) for native file services.
Six slots, the4096-byte runtime prefix and65536-byte runtime body still fit
inside the original1MiB bundle. Actual offsets are recorded in the header;
the current kernel validates the new arrangement before calling any image.
The native Zero builder assembles streams directly; no intermediate disk
images or shell/Python builder is required. ISO/FAT extents are unchanged.
